thanks everyone for coming so at the  office of digital dissemination the  approach we've always taken to digital  dissemination is one of platform  neutrality which sounds like a fancy  term but really what that means is that  when we work with Sheree Carter galvan  who I see here and her colleagues at the  Office of General Counsel to negotiate  agreements for platforms those  agreements are always non-exclusive all  right so what does that mean that means  on one hand that it gives us the richest  set of options to support faculty in  what they envisioned so this allowed us  about five years ago to work with the  Divinity School to use the open-source  Drupal platform to publish teaching  materials to the world with the Miroslav  Volf faith and globalization course when  we think about the open yo courses  initiative it allows us to disseminate  teaching materials on youtube and itunes  in addition to diana's open your courses  yell that edu home website and now as we  think about the future so Paul was just  talking about how will be using Coursera  to start launching MOOCs in early 2014  but again we know that this is in no way  the end game we know there will be more  platforms more technologies and most  importantly faculty will have more  amazing ideas for how they want to  disseminate their teaching materials  that will not fit into what we now  consider this packaged MOOC format one  of those faculty recently contacted  craig and i was YG Dimock who's going to  speak momentarily about an idea that she  has for disseminating teaching materials  that wouldn't be appropriate for a MOOC  platform whether that platform is  Coursera or the open EDX platform out of  Stanford MIT and Harvard but really  needs to rely on other open source tools  whether that be Drupal or WordPress and  call on some of the other broad  dissemination tools like youtube and  itunes so it's a way of sharing our  teaching materials in the world but not  in the way that I think is Diana  described as the coin of the realm now  with the MOOC format so at the core of  this is working with faculty whether  it's at the college the graduate of  professional schools to think about the  goals for that initiative how do you  want to share your teaching materials  who do you want to reach and then let's  look at this broad set of platform  solutions we have and think about which  ones fit because in many cases i think  is why she is going to describe it's not  just one tool that will solve  our goal but it's multiple tools that  she's going to call on so if you have an  idea faculty member again the college or  any the professional schools that  doesn't fit into a Coursera or an open  EDX please contact craig in myself and  we'd love to talk to you about these  solutions that are at our disposal so  why cheat welcome you to come on up and  talk about your idea
 

